    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "While you can share a parameter using the Systems Manager [[p0]] operation, we recommend using Resource Access Manager (RAM) instead. This is because using [[p1]] requires the extra step of promoting the parameter to a standard RAM Resource Share using the RAM [[p2]] API operation. Otherwise, the parameter won’t be returned by the Systems Manager [[p3]] API operation using the [[p4]] option. For more information, see [[p5]] in the [[p6]]Amazon Web Services Systems Manager User Guide[[p7]]",
